<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for ReCut.app itself (package.json -> build.mac.entitlements), used when the app is signed with the
  hardened runtime (a Developer ID build, docs/MACOS-SIGNING.md). Keep this list as short as possible: every
  entitlement weakens the hardened runtime.

  com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
    Required. V8 (JavaScript and the OCR WebAssembly core) compiles code at run time into MAP_JIT memory; without
    this the app crashes at launch. It is the only entitlement in @electron/osx-sign's default set that ReCut needs.

  Deliberately NOT included:
    com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory  not needed: Electron 12+ uses MAP_JIT (allow-jit) on
                                                             macOS. Add it only if a signed build crashes in V8.
    com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation        not needed: every Mach-O in the app (Electron, its
                                                             helpers, ffmpeg, ffprobe) is signed with the same team ID,
                                                             ReCut has no native Node modules, and the bundled FFmpeg
                                                             loads only Apple's system libraries.
    device / personal-information entitlements               ReCut records nothing (no camera, microphone, location).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
